      "data": {
        "text": "**Initiating DynamoDB Integration**\n\nI'm starting the NoSQL document store integration, beginning with `database_client.py` and `database_models.py`. These foundational files are essential for building the `upsert_document.py` functionality using AWS DynamoDB as the concrete implementation. I aim to establish a solid base for seamless data interaction.\n\n\n**Defining Data Structures**\n\nI've begun defining the data models within `database_models.py`, opting for simple dictionary structures for `Document` and `Record` as a starting point. Moving on to `database_client.py`, the plan is to implement the AWS DynamoDB client initialization, leveraging `boto3` and environment variables for region and table name. Next, I'll turn my attention to `upsert_document.py` to get this key function built.\n\n\n**Outlining Data Structures**\n\nI'm focusing now on `database_models.py`, deciding on dictionary-based structures for `Document` and `Record` as initial simple models. This file will be the foundation. Moving on to `database_client.py`, the plan is to establish the DynamoDB client with `boto3`, getting that base implemented. After this, I'll progress to `upsert_document.py`.\n\n\n",
