    {
      "data": {
        "text": "**Implementing Remaining Files**\n\nI'm now implementing the final files, starting with `fetch_document.py`, which I'll build using AWS DynamoDB as the data provider. After that, I will move on to the `query_documents.py` file, continuing with the same scenario and making sure to complete it by using external providers.\n\n\n**Defining External Providers**\n\nI am now outlining the implementation plan for the remaining files. I will use a concrete external provider for each \"scored\" file. I'll use AWS DynamoDB for `fetch_document.py` and `query_documents.py`, and `conditional_update.py`. For later steps, I'll use AWS Comprehend for `record_summary.py` and `record_text_safety.py`. Furthermore, I'll use AWS Translate for `record_translate.py` and AWS S3 for `record_export_archive.py`. I'll start with `fetch_document.py` next.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789845565771,
          "start": 1789845563717
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
